1
00:00:05,547 --> 00:00:06,548
HEY.

2
00:00:06,548 --> 00:00:08,509
Both:
HEY.

3
00:00:08,509 --> 00:00:09,718
WHAT ARE YOU GUYS DOING UP?

4
00:00:09,718 --> 00:00:10,928
OH, WE WANTED TO FINISH
THE CROSSWORD

5
00:00:10,928 --> 00:00:13,096
BEFORE WE
WENT TO BED.

6
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:15,014
DO YOU KNOW
A SIX-LETTER WORD FOR RED?

7
00:00:16,809 --> 00:00:18,059
DARK RED.

8
00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:20,813
YEAH, I THINK
THAT'S WRONG

9
00:00:20,813 --> 00:00:25,024
BUT THERE'S A CONNECT-THE-DOTS
IN HERE FOR YOU LATER.

10
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:26,401
HEY, HOW ABOUT MAROON?

11
00:00:28,487 --> 00:00:31,824
YES. YOU ARE SO SMART.

12
00:00:31,824 --> 00:00:33,993
AH.
YOU GUYS ARE SO CUTE.

13
00:00:33,993 --> 00:00:35,911
I KNOW.

14
00:00:35,911 --> 00:00:38,121
ALL RIGHT, I'LL SEE YOU
IN THE MORNING.

15
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:40,165
OKAY.
OKAY.

16
00:00:52,469 --> 00:00:55,055
I LOVE DOING CROSSWORD
PUZZLES WITH YOU, HONEY.

17
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:56,390
AH. ME, TOO.

18
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:58,058
LET'S FINISH THIS
AND GO TO BED.

19
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,309
OKAY.

20
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:00,561
THERE'S ONLY ONE LEFT.

21
00:01:00,561 --> 00:01:02,062
THREE-LETTER WORD...

22
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:05,566
NOT DOG, BUT..

23
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:08,193
CAT.

24
00:01:08,193 --> 00:01:09,904
YES!

25
00:01:09,904 --> 00:01:14,241
YOU ARE SO SMART.

26
00:01:14,241 --> 00:01:15,534
I LOVE YOU.

27
00:01:15,534 --> 00:01:17,160
I LOVE YOU, TOO.

28
00:01:36,137 --> 00:01:41,142
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

29
00:01:41,142 --> 00:01:43,144
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

30
00:01:43,144 --> 00:01:46,189
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

31
00:01:46,189 --> 00:01:50,778
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

32
00:01:50,778 --> 00:01:53,113
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

33
00:01:53,113 --> 00:01:55,741
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

34
00:01:55,741 --> 00:01:59,369
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

35
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:01,455
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

36
00:02:01,455 --> 00:02:04,458
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

37
00:02:04,458 --> 00:02:05,918
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

38
00:02:05,918 --> 00:02:09,630
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

39
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:13,425
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

40
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:22,726
UH...

41
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:23,727
WE STILL
NEED A TIP.

42
00:02:23,727 --> 00:02:25,270
ALL RIGHT.

43
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:26,480
HOLD ON.

44
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,816
I GOT IT.

45
00:02:28,816 --> 00:02:30,985
NICKEL.

46
00:02:30,985 --> 00:02:32,527
HOW MUCH MORE DO WE NEED?

47
00:02:32,527 --> 00:02:34,237
COUPLE OF BUCKS.

48
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:36,657
OKAY, DIME.

49
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:37,699
YOU GUYS SHOULD PROBABLY
KEEP TALKING.

50
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:38,993
THIS COULD TAKE AWHILE.

51
00:02:38,993 --> 00:02:40,869
OH, NO, WAIT!
LOOKIT!

52
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:42,412
WHOA!

53
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:43,413
OH, MY GOD.

54
00:02:43,413 --> 00:02:45,582
THIS IS A POLICE BADGE.

55
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:46,750
WHY WOULD A COP
COME IN HERE, THOUGH?

56
00:02:46,750 --> 00:02:48,877
THEY DON'T SERVE DOUGHNUTS.

57
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:52,589
COULD YOU DISCOVER
THE BADGE AGAIN?

58
00:02:52,589 --> 00:02:54,842
I THINK I CAN COME
UP WITH SOMETHING
BETTER THAN THAT.

59
00:02:56,677 --> 00:02:58,095
I BET SOMEBODY'S
MISSING THAT BADGE.

60
00:02:58,095 --> 00:02:59,763
YEAH, I SHOULD PROBABLY
TAKE IT BACK.

61
00:02:59,763 --> 00:03:02,016
OOH, BUT YOU KNOW WHAT?
WHILE I'M AT THE POLICE STATION

62
00:03:02,016 --> 00:03:04,018
I COULD CHECK THEIR
TEN MOST WANTED LIST.

63
00:03:04,018 --> 00:03:06,728
'CAUSE MY FRIEND FRITZY'S BEEN
NUMBER 11 FOR, LIKE, EVER

64
00:03:06,728 --> 00:03:07,896
SO THIS COULD BE HER YEAR.

65
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:11,441
HEY, YOU GUYS.

66
00:03:11,441 --> 00:03:12,693
HEY, JOEY.

67
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:13,694
HEY.

68
00:03:13,694 --> 00:03:15,194
HI.

69
00:03:15,194 --> 00:03:17,405
IS THAT, UH...
IS THAT MY SWEATSHIRT?

70
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:18,406
OH, YES, IT IS.

71
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:19,574
I'M SORRY. I BORROWED IT.

72
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:21,368
I WAS COLD.
I-I HOPE IT'S OKAY.

73
00:03:21,368 --> 00:03:23,411
UH, WELL, IT'S JUST THAT, UH...

74
00:03:23,411 --> 00:03:25,330
YOU KNOW, IF YOU'RE GOING TO BE
WEARING SOMEONE'S SWEATSHIRT

75
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:27,708
SHOULDN'T IT BE
YOUR BOYFRIEND'S?

76
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:30,794
YOU KNOW... AND I'M NOT HIM.

77
00:03:30,794 --> 00:03:32,087
I'M SORRY. I'LL GIVE IT
BACK TO YOU.

78
00:03:32,087 --> 00:03:33,088
NO, NO.

79
00:03:33,088 --> 00:03:34,381
NO. IT'S GOING TO BE

80
00:03:34,381 --> 00:03:37,216
ALL SMELLING LIKE MONICA.

81
00:03:37,216 --> 00:03:38,426
ARE YOU SAYING I SMELL BAD?

82
00:03:38,426 --> 00:03:41,847
NO. NO, YOU SMELL LIKE
A MEADOW.

83
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:45,308
I'M SORRY. I...

84
00:03:47,686 --> 00:03:49,646
WHAT'S WITH HIM?

85
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:51,648
OH, YOU KNOW WHAT?
THE LAST TIME THAT JOEY WENT
TO A MEADOW

86
00:03:51,648 --> 00:03:55,485
HIS MOTHER WAS SHOT BY A HUNTER.

87
00:04:07,748 --> 00:04:09,332
OH!

88
00:04:11,459 --> 00:04:13,545
YEAH, I STILL DON'T KNOW.

89
00:04:13,545 --> 00:04:16,255
I'M SORRY, I JUST WANT TO MAKE
SURE I BOUGHT THE RIGHT COUCH.

90
00:04:16,255 --> 00:04:18,133
I NEED A COUCH THAT SAYS

91
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:19,718
"KIDS WELCOME HERE"

92
00:04:19,718 --> 00:04:22,596
BUT THAT ALSO SAYS...

93
00:04:22,596 --> 00:04:25,140
"COME HERE TO ME."

94
00:04:27,226 --> 00:04:28,309
WHAT?

95
00:04:28,309 --> 00:04:30,604
YOU SAY THAT TO KIDS?

96
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:31,939
NO, NO, NO.

97
00:04:31,939 --> 00:04:34,066
THE "COME HERE TO ME" IS...

98
00:04:34,066 --> 00:04:35,859
YOU KNOW, FOR THE LADIES.

99
00:04:37,444 --> 00:04:39,113
ROSS, HONEY,
IT'S A NICE COUCH.

100
00:04:39,113 --> 00:04:40,614
IT'S NOT A MAGIC COUCH.

101
00:04:42,365 --> 00:04:43,909
YOU PICKED
A GREAT COUCH.

102
00:04:43,909 --> 00:04:45,160
YEAH?

103
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,912
COULD YOU SIGN
HERE, PLEASE?

104
00:04:46,912 --> 00:04:48,622
WHOA, WHOA. WHAT'S...?

105
00:04:48,622 --> 00:04:52,084
THE DELIVERY CHARGE IS ALMOST
AS MUCH AS THE COUCH.

106
00:04:52,084 --> 00:04:53,543
WAIT, NO. THAT'S RIDICULOUS.

107
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:55,378
COME ON, HE LIVES
THREE BLOCKS AWAY.

108
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:56,671
YEAH, YOU KNOW WHAT?

109
00:04:56,671 --> 00:04:58,339
I'LL TAKE IT
MYSELF, THANK YOU.

110
00:04:58,339 --> 00:05:00,217
ALL RIGHT, RACH, COME ON.
LET'S GO.

111
00:05:00,217 --> 00:05:01,969
YEAH.

112
00:05:05,597 --> 00:05:07,306
( laughing )

113
00:05:07,306 --> 00:05:09,851
ARE YOU KIDDING?

114
00:05:09,851 --> 00:05:11,603
NO, COME ON.
IT'S ONLY THREE BLOCKS.

115
00:05:11,603 --> 00:05:13,021
IT'S NOT VERY HEAVY.

116
00:05:13,021 --> 00:05:14,189
TRY IT. COME ON.

117
00:05:14,189 --> 00:05:16,150
( frustrated grunt )

118
00:05:18,735 --> 00:05:20,361
OH! OH, I CAN DO IT.

119
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:21,738
YEAH.

120
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:23,323
YOU TWO WILL REALLY
ENJOY THAT COUCH.

121
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:24,866
OH, YEAH,
WE'RE, UH...

122
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:26,660
YEAH, WE'RE
NOT TOGETHER.

123
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:28,411
OH. OKAY.

124
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:29,871
( laughing )

125
00:05:29,871 --> 00:05:31,290
SOMETHING DIDN'T
QUITE ADD UP THERE.

126
00:05:36,753 --> 00:05:38,130
ROSS...

127
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:39,422
WHAT'S THAT
SUPPOSED TO MEAN?

128
00:05:39,422 --> 00:05:40,841
ROSS...

129
00:05:40,841 --> 00:05:43,635
YOU... HER...

130
00:05:43,635 --> 00:05:45,470
I MEAN, SHE'S VERY...

131
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:47,097
YOU KNOW...

132
00:05:47,097 --> 00:05:48,849
AND YOU'RE LIKE...

133
00:05:48,849 --> 00:05:50,684
YOU KNOW...

134
00:05:52,936 --> 00:05:57,149
NOT THAT IT'S ANY OF YOUR
BUSINESS, BUT WE DID GO OUT.

135
00:05:57,149 --> 00:05:58,317
REALLY? YOU TWO?

136
00:05:58,317 --> 00:05:59,985
YEAH. RACH?

137
00:05:59,985 --> 00:06:01,444
I REALLY DON'T WANT
TO BE DOING THIS RIGHT NOW.

138
00:06:01,444 --> 00:06:03,947
I'M CARRYING A VERY HEAVY COUCH.

139
00:06:03,947 --> 00:06:06,741
THEN TELL HIM QUICKLY.

140
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:08,493
FINE. WE WENT OUT.

141
00:06:08,493 --> 00:06:10,954
NOT ONLY DID WE GO OUT

142
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:14,082
WE DID IT... 298 TIMES.

143
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:16,084
ROSS!

144
00:06:16,084 --> 00:06:18,086
OH, MY...

145
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:20,088
OH! YOU KEPT COUNT?!

146
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:22,090
YOU ARE SUCH A LOSER.

147
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:27,012
A LOSER YOU DID IT WITH
298 TIMES.

148
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:32,893
OH! OH!

149
00:06:32,893 --> 00:06:33,894
MA'AM! EXCUSE ME, MA'AM?

150
00:06:33,894 --> 00:06:35,436
YES?

151
00:06:35,436 --> 00:06:37,898
YOU CAN'T PUT YOUR
CIGARETTE OUT ON A TREE.

152
00:06:37,898 --> 00:06:39,774
YEAH, I CAN.
IT WORKED REAL WELL.

153
00:06:39,774 --> 00:06:41,526
NO, BUT YOU SHOULDN'T.

154
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:43,737
SO DON'T EVER DO THAT AGAIN.

155
00:06:43,737 --> 00:06:44,988
I WON'T...

156
00:06:44,988 --> 00:06:47,157
TILL I HAVE MY NEXT CIGARETTE.

157
00:06:47,157 --> 00:06:48,491
HOLD IT.

158
00:06:48,491 --> 00:06:50,493
N.Y.P.D.
FREEZE, PUNK.

159
00:06:50,493 --> 00:06:52,079
WHAT?

160
00:06:52,079 --> 00:06:53,538
YEAH, THAT'S RIGHT.

161
00:06:53,538 --> 00:06:55,082
YOU ARE SO BUSTED.

162
00:06:55,082 --> 00:06:56,083
( laughing )

163
00:06:56,083 --> 00:06:57,209
UH, BOOK 'EM.

164
00:06:59,211 --> 00:07:00,419
WHO ARE YOU TALKING TO?

165
00:07:00,419 --> 00:07:02,339
SAVE IT, RED!

166
00:07:02,339 --> 00:07:04,174
UNLESS YOU WANT TO SPEND
THE NIGHT IN THE SLAMMER

167
00:07:04,174 --> 00:07:06,927
YOU APOLOGIZE TO THE TREE.

168
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:10,013
I AM NOT GOING TO
APOLOGIZE TO A TREE.

169
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:11,681
YOU APOLOGIZE TO
THE TREE RIGHT NOW

170
00:07:11,681 --> 00:07:13,558
OR I AM CALLING FOR BACKUP.

171
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:17,271
BACKUP! BACKUP!

172
00:07:17,271 --> 00:07:19,189
I-I'M SORRY! SORRY!

173
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:20,274
OKAY, CANCEL BACKUP!

174
00:07:20,274 --> 00:07:23,235
CANCEL BACKUP!

175
00:07:23,235 --> 00:07:25,320
OKAY.

176
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:28,656
ROSS, DIDN'T YOU SAY
THAT THERE WAS AN
ELEVATOR IN HERE?

177
00:07:28,656 --> 00:07:30,158
UH, YES, I DID, BUT THERE ISN'T.

178
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:31,450
OKAY, HERE WE GO.

179
00:07:33,287 --> 00:07:35,289
OKAY, GO LEFT. LEFT.

180
00:07:35,289 --> 00:07:36,623
OKAY.

181
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:37,916
LEFT!

182
00:07:37,916 --> 00:07:39,293
OKAY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

183
00:07:39,293 --> 00:07:40,752
THERE'S NO MORE LEFT LEFT.

184
00:07:40,752 --> 00:07:42,212
OH, OKAY.

185
00:07:42,212 --> 00:07:44,339
YOU KNOW, LIFT IT STRAIGHT UP
OVER YOUR HEAD.

186
00:07:44,339 --> 00:07:45,590
STRAIGHT UP OVER YOUR HEAD.

187
00:07:45,590 --> 00:07:46,591
YOU CAN DO IT.

188
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:47,592
YOU CAN DO IT.

189
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:48,593
( grunting )

190
00:07:48,593 --> 00:07:49,761
OKAY. YOU GOT IT?

191
00:07:49,761 --> 00:07:51,305
YEAH. GO. GO.

192
00:07:51,305 --> 00:07:53,265
OKAY, YOU GOT IT, RIGHT?
YOU GOT IT, RIGHT?

193
00:07:53,265 --> 00:07:54,266
RIGHT. YEAH.

194
00:07:54,266 --> 00:07:55,392
( screams )

195
00:07:59,562 --> 00:08:02,065
ANY CHANCE YOU THINK THE
COUCH LOOKS GOOD THERE?

196
00:08:04,151 --> 00:08:05,402
SO, THIS GUY WAS ALL

197
00:08:05,402 --> 00:08:06,903
( mumbles )

198
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:08,905
AND I'M ALL,
"BUFFAY. HOMICIDE."

199
00:08:10,489 --> 00:08:12,491
IT WAS JUST SO COOL.

200
00:08:12,491 --> 00:08:14,661
PHOEBE, YOU WERE
SUPPOSED TO TAKE
THAT BACK.

201
00:08:14,661 --> 00:08:18,248
I KNOW, BUT I'M HAVING
SO MUCH FUN DOING GOOD DEEDS.

202
00:08:18,248 --> 00:08:20,667
OKAY, BUT IMPERSONATING A POLICE
OFFICER'S A SERIOUS THING.

203
00:08:20,667 --> 00:08:22,210
YOU COULD GET ARRESTED.

204
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:24,212
YOU COULD GET ARRESTED
RIGHT NOW.

205
00:08:27,341 --> 00:08:29,550
ALL RIGHT, YEAH,
I BETTER TAKE IT BACK.

206
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:30,718
TOTALLY DRUNK WITH POWER.

207
00:08:33,805 --> 00:08:34,806
HEY.

208
00:08:34,806 --> 00:08:37,434
HEY.

209
00:08:37,434 --> 00:08:40,228
OH, I...

210
00:08:40,228 --> 00:08:41,562
HI, JOE.

211
00:08:41,562 --> 00:08:42,605
I DIDN'T KNOW YOU GUYS

212
00:08:42,605 --> 00:08:44,065
WERE GOING TO BE HERE.

213
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:45,484
HEY, JOEY?
DO ME A FAVOR, SWEETIE.
TASTE THIS.

214
00:08:45,484 --> 00:08:48,278
WHAT? WHY?

215
00:08:48,278 --> 00:08:50,071
WHAT IS GOING ON
WITH YOU?
NOTHING.

216
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:52,531
YOU'VE BEEN ACTING STRANGE
ALL DAY.

217
00:08:52,531 --> 00:08:53,533
ALL RIGHT.

218
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:54,534
THERE IS SOMETHING.

219
00:08:54,534 --> 00:08:56,495
I, UH...

220
00:08:56,495 --> 00:08:59,580
I KIND OF HAD A DREAM...

221
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:00,790
BUT I DON'T WANT TO TALK
ABOUT IT.

222
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,209
WHOA, WHOA,
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA!

223
00:09:02,209 --> 00:09:04,461
WHAT IF MARTIN LUTHER KING
HAD SAID THAT?

224
00:09:06,505 --> 00:09:09,007
I... KIND OF HAVE A DREAM.

225
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:14,388
I DON'T WANT TO
TALK ABOUT IT.

226
00:09:14,388 --> 00:09:16,597
IT INVOLVED MONICA.

227
00:09:16,597 --> 00:09:19,267
YOU HAD A DREAM ABOUT
A GIRL THAT I'M SEEING?
OH, THAT IS SO COOL.

228
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:22,020
SO MANY TIMES I DREAMT
ABOUT A GIRL THAT
HE WAS SEEING.

229
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:23,063
ANYWAY, WE'RE TALKING
ABOUT YOUR DREAM.

230
00:09:23,063 --> 00:09:25,815
I LOVE YOU. YOUR DREAM?

231
00:09:25,815 --> 00:09:27,942
THERE WASN'T ANY SEX IN IT
OR ANYTHING.

232
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:29,361
I HAVEN'T DREAMT ABOUT HER
LIKE THAT

233
00:09:29,361 --> 00:09:32,155
SINCE I FOUND OUT ABOUT
YOU TWO... ISH.

234
00:09:36,868 --> 00:09:38,495
WHAT WAS THE DREAM ABOUT?

235
00:09:38,495 --> 00:09:41,248
WELL... OKAY.

236
00:09:41,248 --> 00:09:43,417
YOU WERE MY GIRLFRIEND

237
00:09:43,417 --> 00:09:45,252
AND WE WERE DOING
THE CROSSWORD PUZZLE--

238
00:09:45,252 --> 00:09:46,420
YOU KNOW, LIKE YOU GUYS
WERE DOING LAST NIGHT.

239
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:48,171
SO, THAT'S IT.

240
00:09:48,171 --> 00:09:50,048
I'M IN LOVE WITH MONICA
AND I'LL BE MOVING OUT.

241
00:09:50,048 --> 00:09:51,883
WAIT, JOEY, JOEY.

242
00:09:51,883 --> 00:09:54,428
THAT DOESN'T MEAN THAT-THAT
YOU'RE IN LOVE WITH ME.

243
00:09:54,428 --> 00:09:56,179
IT... IT DOESN'T?

244
00:09:56,179 --> 00:09:58,014
NO, IT CAN
MEAN ANYTHING...

245
00:09:58,014 --> 00:09:59,558
LIKE ALL OF A SUDDEN
YOU'RE JEALOUS

246
00:09:59,558 --> 00:10:02,727
THAT I'VE BECOME
THE APARTMENT STUD.

247
00:10:02,727 --> 00:10:04,396
KIND OF SOUNDS LIKE
YOUR DREAM, DUDE.

248
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:09,484
OR IT COULD MEAN THAT YOU SAW
CHANDLER AND ME TOGETHER

249
00:10:09,484 --> 00:10:11,861
AND WE WERE BEING
CLOSE AND STUFF

250
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:14,155
AND-AND YOU JUST WANT
TO HAVE THAT WITH SOMEONE, TOO.

251
00:10:14,155 --> 00:10:16,199
WELL, IN THE DREAM,
I DID ENJOY THE CLOSENESS.

252
00:10:16,199 --> 00:10:17,200
Monica:
MM-HMM.

253
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,201
OKAY, LOOK, LOOK.

254
00:10:18,201 --> 00:10:19,702
ARE YOU ATTRACTED TO MONICA?

255
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:22,414
RIGHT HERE, RIGHT NOW,
ARE YOU ATTRACTED TO HER?

256
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:26,334
NOT REALLY.

257
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:28,086
WELL, THERE YOU HAVE IT.

258
00:10:28,086 --> 00:10:32,840
WELL, SURE, I'M JUST
WEARING SWEATS.

259
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:34,175
BUT THAT'S GOOD...

260
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:35,302
THAT YOU'RE NOT
IN LOVE WITH ME

261
00:10:35,302 --> 00:10:37,429
BECAUSE YOU JUST
WANT A GIRLFRIEND.

262
00:10:37,429 --> 00:10:38,930
NO, I DON'T THINK
IT'S JUST ABOUT

263
00:10:38,930 --> 00:10:40,599
JUST GETTING A GIRLFRIEND,
YOU KNOW?

264
00:10:40,599 --> 00:10:42,392
I MEAN, YEAH, I COULD
GET A GIRLFRIEND.

265
00:10:42,392 --> 00:10:44,685
YEAH, WE COULD SIT IN THE CHAIR
AND DO CROSSWORD PUZZLES

266
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:48,773
BUT WILL WE EVER HAVE THE
CLOSENESS LIKE YOU GUYS HAVE?

267
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:50,317
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT?
MONICA AND I WERE FRIENDS

268
00:10:50,317 --> 00:10:51,318
BEFORE WE STARTED DATING

269
00:10:51,318 --> 00:10:52,651
SO MAYBE THAT'S IT.

270
00:10:52,651 --> 00:10:54,988
FRIENDS FIRST?

271
00:10:54,988 --> 00:10:56,615
THAT'S INTERESTING.

272
00:10:56,615 --> 00:10:57,616
( chuckles )

273
00:10:57,616 --> 00:10:58,950
YOU BECOME FRIENDS AFTER?

274
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:00,910
NO. NEVER DONE THAT, EITHER.

275
00:11:02,579 --> 00:11:04,956
HEY... UM, DO YOU GUYS
HAVE A TAPE MEASURE?

276
00:11:04,956 --> 00:11:06,833
OH, YEAH, IT'S ACTUALLY
IN MY BEDROOM.

277
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:08,835
( giggling )

278
00:11:08,835 --> 00:11:10,629
THAT'S RIGHT.

279
00:11:22,849 --> 00:11:24,809
WHAT'S UP, JOEY?

280
00:11:27,686 --> 00:11:29,189
HOW YOU DOIN'?

281
00:11:38,532 --> 00:11:41,201
OH... EXCUSE ME.
IS THIS YOUR CAR?
YEAH.

282
00:11:41,201 --> 00:11:43,077
I DON'T THINK IT'S
VERY NICE OF YOU TO PARK HERE.

283
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:44,703
YOU'RE BLOCKING THE ENTRANCE.

284
00:11:44,703 --> 00:11:46,581
DON'T WORRY ABOUT IT.
IT'S NOT A PROBLEM.

285
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:48,249
WELL, IT'S A PROBLEM FOR ME

286
00:11:48,249 --> 00:11:50,001
WHICH MEANS
IT'S A PROBLEM FOR YOU

287
00:11:50,001 --> 00:11:52,379
'CAUSE I'M A COP.

288
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:55,131
SO AM I.

289
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:59,678
OH, NO.

290
00:12:01,762 --> 00:12:03,722
OH, OKAY, SO YOU'RE A COP

291
00:12:03,722 --> 00:12:05,475
WHICH MEANS
YOU CAN PARK ANYWHERE.

292
00:12:05,475 --> 00:12:07,602
I KNOW THAT,
'CAUSE I'M A COP, TOO.

293
00:12:07,602 --> 00:12:09,937
SORRY. KEEP UP THE GOOD WORK.
TEN-FOUR.

294
00:12:09,937 --> 00:12:11,189
HEY, WAIT A SECOND.

295
00:12:11,189 --> 00:12:12,899
SO WHAT PRECINCT
ARE YOU WITH?

296
00:12:12,899 --> 00:12:15,694
I-I'M WITH THE, UM, THE 57th.

297
00:12:15,694 --> 00:12:17,445
OH, I KNOW A GUY IN
HOMICIDE UP THERE.

298
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:18,821
I'M IN VICE.

299
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:21,282
YEAH, IN FACT, I'M
UNDERCOVER RIGHT NOW.

300
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:25,245
I'M A WHORE.

301
00:12:25,245 --> 00:12:27,038
WHO ELSE IS IN
VICE UP THERE?

302
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:30,458
UM, DO YOU KNOW,
UM, SIPOWITZ?

303
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:33,503
SIPOWITZ? NO,
I DON'T THINK SO.

304
00:12:33,503 --> 00:12:35,004
YEAH, SIPOWITZ, YEAH.

305
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:36,755
BIG GUY, KIND OF BALD.

306
00:12:36,755 --> 00:12:38,132
NAH, I DON'T KNOW HIM.

307
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:40,218
OKAY.

308
00:12:40,218 --> 00:12:41,636
DON'T TRY
TO CALL HIM OR ANYTHING

309
00:12:41,636 --> 00:12:43,096
'CAUSE HE'S NOT THERE.

310
00:12:43,096 --> 00:12:44,264
HE'S OUT.

311
00:12:44,264 --> 00:12:46,266
HIS, UM...
HIS PARTNER JUST DIED.

312
00:12:46,266 --> 00:12:50,311
WOW. WELL, TELL SIPOWITZ
I'M REAL SORRY FOR HIS LOSS.

313
00:12:50,311 --> 00:12:52,063
I-I SURE WILL.
TAKE CARE.

314
00:12:52,063 --> 00:12:53,064
OKAY.

315
00:12:53,064 --> 00:12:54,608
HEY, BY THE WAY

316
00:12:54,608 --> 00:12:56,067
I'M SURE SIPOWITZ IS
GOING TO BE ALL RIGHT.

317
00:12:56,067 --> 00:12:57,569
I HEARD THAT KID
FROM SILVER SPOONS

318
00:12:57,569 --> 00:13:02,031
IS REALLY GOOD.

319
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:04,200
AND WHERE'D YOU
FIND MY BADGE?

320
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,826
OH.

321
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:15,295
HEY, JOEY,
WOULD YOU MIND

322
00:13:15,295 --> 00:13:18,339
GIVING ME AND ROSS
A HAND MOVING HIS COUCH?

323
00:13:18,339 --> 00:13:20,174
OH, I'D LOVE TO,
BUT I GOT ACTING CLASS.

324
00:13:20,174 --> 00:13:21,175
BUT YOU KNOW WHAT?

325
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:22,801
I GUESS I COULD BLOW THAT OFF...

326
00:13:22,801 --> 00:13:24,095
FOR YOU.

327
00:13:29,016 --> 00:13:30,435
THANKS.

328
00:13:30,435 --> 00:13:32,145
UH, SAY, RACHEL, LET
ME ASK YOU SOMETHING.

329
00:13:32,145 --> 00:13:33,354
UH, I WAS JUST OVER THERE

330
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:34,855
TALKING TO MONICA
AND CHANDLER

331
00:13:34,855 --> 00:13:36,316
AND, BOY, THEY
ARE REALLY TIGHT.

332
00:13:36,316 --> 00:13:38,109
I KNOW.

333
00:13:38,109 --> 00:13:40,194
THAT'S NOT A BAD SITUATION
THEY GOT GOING OVER THERE.

334
00:13:40,194 --> 00:13:41,904
UH-UH.

335
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:44,324
THINKING OF GETTING ME
ONE OF THOSE.

336
00:13:46,493 --> 00:13:49,370
WHAT'S UP, JOE?

337
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:51,790
WELL, THE REASON I THINK
MONICA AND CHANDLER

338
00:13:51,790 --> 00:13:56,002
ARE SO GREAT IS BECAUSE THEY
WERE FRIENDS FIRST, YOU KNOW?

339
00:13:56,002 --> 00:13:58,254
SO I ASKED MYSELF,
WHO ARE MY FRIENDS?

340
00:13:58,254 --> 00:14:00,674
YOU AND PHOEBE.

341
00:14:00,674 --> 00:14:04,427
I SAW YOU FIRST, SO...

342
00:14:04,427 --> 00:14:05,470
( nervous laughing )

343
00:14:05,470 --> 00:14:07,138
WHAT ARE YOU SAYING?

344
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:10,433
I'M SAYING, MAYBE YOU AND I
CRANK IT UP A NOTCH.

345
00:14:14,354 --> 00:14:18,857
YOU KNOW, HONEY, UM, AS, UH...
AS FLATTERED AS I AM

346
00:14:18,857 --> 00:14:22,945
THAT YOU SAW ME FIRST,
UH, I JUST...

347
00:14:22,945 --> 00:14:27,408
I DON'T THINK WE SHOULD BE
CRANKING ANYTHING UP.

348
00:14:27,408 --> 00:14:29,661
WELL, I'LL TREAT
YOU REAL NICE.

349
00:14:34,165 --> 00:14:36,125
OH-HO.

350
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:39,420
YEAH, WELL,
YOU KNOW, UM...

351
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:42,590
NO, HONEY, LISTEN, I THINK
IT'S A GREAT IDEA TO BECOME

352
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:44,843
FRIENDS WITH SOMEONE
BEFORE YOU DATE THEM

353
00:14:44,843 --> 00:14:47,637
BUT THE WAY YOU DO IT IS,
YOU KNOW, YOU MEET SOMEONE

354
00:14:47,637 --> 00:14:50,931
BECOME THEIR FRIEND,
BUILD A FOUNDATION

355
00:14:50,931 --> 00:14:52,933
THEN ASK THEM
OUT ON A DATE.

356
00:14:52,933 --> 00:14:57,271
DON'T HIT ON
YOUR EXISTING FRIENDS.

357
00:14:57,271 --> 00:15:00,483
WELL, WON'T THAT
TAKE LONGER?

358
00:15:00,483 --> 00:15:02,360
YEAH. YEAH.

359
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:06,614
OH, BUT ONCE YOU FIND IT,
OH, IT'S SO WORTH THE WAIT.

360
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:09,701
YEAH.
WELL, I UNDERSTAND.

361
00:15:09,701 --> 00:15:12,328
I UNDERSTAND,
YOU KNOW.

362
00:15:12,328 --> 00:15:15,289
MAN, I WISH I
SAW PHOEBE FIRST.

363
00:15:18,376 --> 00:15:21,671
COME HERE TO ME.

364
00:15:21,671 --> 00:15:25,091
NO, NO. YOU COME HERE TO ME.

365
00:15:25,091 --> 00:15:26,509
HEY, ROSS.

366
00:15:26,509 --> 00:15:27,677
( clearing throat )

367
00:15:27,677 --> 00:15:28,969
I BROUGHT REINFORCEMENTS.

368
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:30,597
OH, GREAT. WHAT,
YOU BROUGHT JOEY?

369
00:15:30,597 --> 00:15:32,181
WELL, I BROUGHT
THE NEXT BEST THING.

370
00:15:32,181 --> 00:15:34,434
HEY.

371
00:15:34,434 --> 00:15:35,976
CHANDLER? YOU
BROUGHT CHANDLER?

372
00:15:35,976 --> 00:15:39,188
THE NEXT BEST THING
WOULD BE MONICA.

373
00:15:39,188 --> 00:15:40,481
YOU KNOW,
I WOULD BE OFFENDED

374
00:15:40,481 --> 00:15:43,067
BUT MONICA IS
FREAKISHLY STRONG, SO...

375
00:15:43,067 --> 00:15:44,903
ALL RIGHT, LOOK,
I-I DREW A SKETCH

376
00:15:44,903 --> 00:15:46,780
OF HOW WE'RE GOING
TO DO IT, OKAY?

377
00:15:46,780 --> 00:15:48,656
RACH, THAT'S YOU.

378
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:50,116
THAT'S THE COUCH.

379
00:15:50,116 --> 00:15:52,535
MM-HMM. OOH, WHAT'S THAT?

380
00:15:52,535 --> 00:15:54,579
OH, THAT'S ME.

381
00:15:54,579 --> 00:15:59,417
WOW.

382
00:15:59,417 --> 00:16:01,586
YOU CERTAINLY THINK
A LOT OF YOURSELF.

383
00:16:03,421 --> 00:16:05,214
NO, THAT'S...
THAT'S MY ARM.

384
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:10,470
OH, I SEE.

385
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:14,265
I THOUGHT YOU JUST REALLY,
REALLY LIKED YOUR NEW COUCH.

386
00:16:16,893 --> 00:16:18,645
YOU KNOW, JUST...
JUST FOLLOW MY LEAD.

387
00:16:18,645 --> 00:16:20,271
OKAY.
OKAY.

388
00:16:20,271 --> 00:16:22,148
COME ON,
CHANDLER.

389
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:24,901
ALL RIGHT.

390
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:25,944
OKAY.

391
00:16:25,944 --> 00:16:27,528
HERE WE GO.

392
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:30,615
ALL RIGHT,
READY, SET, TURN.

393
00:16:30,615 --> 00:16:31,616
OKAY.

394
00:16:31,616 --> 00:16:33,326
TURN.

395
00:16:33,326 --> 00:16:34,327
TURN.

396
00:16:34,327 --> 00:16:35,703
( screaming )

397
00:16:35,703 --> 00:16:37,705
I DON'T THINK WE
CAN TURN ANYMORE.

398
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:39,039
ROSS, I JUST
DON'T THINK

399
00:16:39,039 --> 00:16:40,040
IT'S GOING TO FIT.

400
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,041
OH, YEAH, IT WILL.

401
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:42,961
COME ON, UP.
UP, UP, UP.

402
00:16:42,961 --> 00:16:44,378
UP!

403
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:46,881
HERE WE GO, PIVOT.

404
00:16:46,881 --> 00:16:49,509
PIVOT!

405
00:16:51,302 --> 00:16:52,261
PIVOT!

406
00:16:53,346 --> 00:16:54,305
PIVOT!

407
00:16:56,098 --> 00:16:57,851
PIVOT!

408
00:16:57,851 --> 00:16:59,853
PIVOT.

409
00:16:59,853 --> 00:17:03,815
SHUT UP! SHUT UP! SHUT UP.

410
00:17:07,109 --> 00:17:09,612
OKAY, I... I DON'T THINK
IT'S GOING TO PIVOT ANYMORE.

411
00:17:09,612 --> 00:17:13,533
YOU THINK?
YOU THINK?

412
00:17:13,533 --> 00:17:14,909
ALL RIGHT, LET'S, UH...

413
00:17:14,909 --> 00:17:17,286
LET'S BRING IT BACK DOWN
AND TRY AGAIN.

414
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:20,122
OKAY. OH...

415
00:17:20,122 --> 00:17:22,583
( grunting and groaning )

416
00:17:25,461 --> 00:17:29,298
OKAY, YEAH. I THINK
IT'S REALLY STUCK NOW.

417
00:17:29,298 --> 00:17:31,384
I CAN'T BELIEVE
THAT DIDN'T WORK.

418
00:17:31,384 --> 00:17:32,886
I KNOW. ME NEITHER.

419
00:17:32,886 --> 00:17:34,929
I MEAN, YOU HAD A SKETCH.

420
00:17:34,929 --> 00:17:37,557
OH, YOU KNOW WHAT?

421
00:17:37,557 --> 00:17:39,392
WHAT DID YOU MEAN
WHEN YOU SAID PIVOT?

422
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:44,271
HEY.

423
00:17:44,271 --> 00:17:45,272
HEY.

424
00:17:45,272 --> 00:17:46,440
HOW'S IT GOING?

425
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,234
DID YOU MAKE
ANY NEW FRIENDS?

426
00:17:48,234 --> 00:17:50,987
YEAH. YEAH, I MET THIS WOMAN.

427
00:17:50,987 --> 00:17:53,072
OKAY, WHOA, WHOA.

428
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:54,240
WHAT'S SHE LIKE?

429
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:55,533
UH, WELL...

430
00:17:55,533 --> 00:17:59,662
SHE'S REALLY GOOD IN BED.

431
00:17:59,662 --> 00:18:00,663
JOEY, I THOUGHT
YOU WERE GOING TO TRY

432
00:18:00,663 --> 00:18:01,789
TO BE FRIENDS FIRST.

433
00:18:01,789 --> 00:18:03,708
WELL, HEY, IT'S ALL YOUR FAULT.

434
00:18:03,708 --> 00:18:05,376
WHAT? WHY?

435
00:18:05,376 --> 00:18:06,920
BECAUSE YOU
DIDN'T GIVE ME ADVICE.

436
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:08,629
NO, YOU GAVE ME
A PICKUP LINE.

437
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:11,007
AS SOON AS I TOLD HER
I WANTED TO BUILD A FOUNDATION

438
00:18:11,007 --> 00:18:12,717
AND BE FRIENDS FIRST

439
00:18:12,717 --> 00:18:15,219
I SUDDENLY--
THROUGH NO FAULT OF MY OWN--

440
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:18,556
BECAME IRRESISTIBLE TO HER.

441
00:18:18,556 --> 00:18:19,766
AND HER ROOMMATE.

442
00:18:22,101 --> 00:18:24,228
WHAT ABOUT
THE CLOSENESS?

443
00:18:24,228 --> 00:18:25,772
CLOSENESS, SCHMOSENESS.

444
00:18:25,772 --> 00:18:27,189
THERE WAS THREE OF US,
FOR CRYING OUT LOUD.

445
00:18:33,111 --> 00:18:34,822
ALL RIGHT, HEY, WHO WANTS PIZZA?

446
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:36,824
I DO. I DO. I DO.

447
00:18:36,824 --> 00:18:38,242
OH, THIS
IS GREAT.

448
00:18:38,242 --> 00:18:40,119
CAN YOU BELIEVE I FOUND THIS
ON THE SECOND FLOOR?

449
00:18:41,328 --> 00:18:43,163
( knocking on door )

450
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:44,415
WHO IS IT?

451
00:18:44,415 --> 00:18:45,959
Man:
N.Y.P.D.

452
00:18:45,959 --> 00:18:47,167
OH, MY GOD.

453
00:18:47,167 --> 00:18:50,088
UH... JUST A MINUTE,
OFFICER!

454
00:18:59,764 --> 00:19:01,808
I'M LOOKING
FOR PHOEBE BUFFAY.

455
00:19:01,808 --> 00:19:03,101
OH, MY GOD, IT'S HIM.

456
00:19:03,101 --> 00:19:04,560
IT'S THAT COP.

457
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:05,895
GOD, I CAN'T BELIEVE IT.
HE FOUND ME.

458
00:19:05,895 --> 00:19:07,063
MY GOD, PHOEBE.

459
00:19:07,063 --> 00:19:08,856
ARE YOU GOING
TO GO TO JAIL?

460
00:19:08,856 --> 00:19:12,777
WELL, IF I'M GOING DOWN,
YOU GUYS ARE GOING DOWN WITH ME.

461
00:19:12,777 --> 00:19:13,778
WHAT?

462
00:19:13,778 --> 00:19:15,113
HARBORING A FUGITIVE?

463
00:19:15,113 --> 00:19:17,991
THAT'S
ONE-TO-THREE YEARS MINIMUM.

464
00:19:17,991 --> 00:19:19,533
GOOD LUCK, CHANDLER.

465
00:19:23,203 --> 00:19:25,414
OKAY, YOU CAN ARREST
ME, FINE, BUT YOU'LL

466
00:19:25,414 --> 00:19:27,207
NEVER MAKE IT STICK,
AND YOU KNOW IT.

467
00:19:27,207 --> 00:19:28,876
YEAH, BUT I
KIND OF DON'T HAVE A CHOICE.

468
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:30,753
IT'S MY JOB. I MEAN,
YOU UNDERSTAND, RIGHT?

469
00:19:30,753 --> 00:19:33,297
YEAH, AS LONG AS YOU UNDERSTAND
THAT I'M GOING TO CALL MY LAWYER

470
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:35,174
AND ONCE HE PUTS YOU
ON THE STAND

471
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:37,844
HE'S GOING TO MAKE YOU LOOK
LIKE A FOOL, LIKE A FOOL.

472
00:19:37,844 --> 00:19:41,597
MM-HMM. I DON'T LIKE
LOOKING FOOLISH.

473
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:44,224
YOU KNOW WHAT? MAYBE, UH,
I DON'T ARREST YOU TODAY.

474
00:19:44,224 --> 00:19:46,226
MAYBE I CAME BY
AND YOU WEREN'T HERE.

475
00:19:46,226 --> 00:19:49,271
I WOULD LOVE IT
IF I WEREN'T HERE.

476
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:51,899
OKAY, SINCE, UM, YOU'RE
NOT GOING TO JAIL TONIGHT

477
00:19:51,899 --> 00:19:53,442
I WAS WONDERING IF
YOU WOULD LIKE

478
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:56,029
TO GO TO DINNER WITH ME.

479
00:19:56,029 --> 00:19:57,030
ME?

480
00:19:57,030 --> 00:19:58,197
YEAH.

481
00:19:58,197 --> 00:19:59,824
EVER SINCE YOU FLASHED
MY BADGE AT ME

482
00:19:59,824 --> 00:20:01,951
I KIND OF CAN'T STOP
THINKING ABOUT YOU.

483
00:20:01,951 --> 00:20:05,038
YOU'RE THE PRETTIEST FAKE
UNDERCOVER WHORE I'VE EVER SEEN.

484
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:09,416
NICE.
NICE.

485
00:20:11,502 --> 00:20:13,253
WOW, I DIDN'T SEE THAT COMING.

486
00:20:13,253 --> 00:20:14,755
YOU'RE ASKING ME OUT.

487
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:16,174
YEAH, AND I COULD
HAVE DONE IT BETTER

488
00:20:16,174 --> 00:20:17,591
BUT THESE PEOPLE
KEEP STARING AT ME.

489
00:20:17,591 --> 00:20:19,301
UM... YEAH.

490
00:20:19,301 --> 00:20:23,806
I-I'D LIKE TO GO OUT
WITH YOU, OFFICER.

491
00:20:23,806 --> 00:20:24,807
GARY.

492
00:20:24,807 --> 00:20:26,017
GARY.

493
00:20:26,017 --> 00:20:27,351
OKAY, SO IT'S A DATE?

494
00:20:27,351 --> 00:20:29,103
YEAH. I GOT TO ASK.

495
00:20:29,103 --> 00:20:30,688
HOW DID YOU KNOW
WHERE TO FIND ME?

496
00:20:30,688 --> 00:20:32,398
YOUR FINGERPRINTS
WERE ALL OVER MY BADGE

497
00:20:32,398 --> 00:20:33,858
SO I RAN THEM
THROUGH THE COMPUTER

498
00:20:33,858 --> 00:20:35,776
AND THIS IS LISTED
AS YOUR LAST KNOWN ADDRESS

499
00:20:35,776 --> 00:20:36,777
SO I CHECKED IT OUT.

500
00:20:36,777 --> 00:20:38,029
OH, IMPRESSIVE.

501
00:20:38,029 --> 00:20:39,279
NOT AS IMPRESSIVE AS YOU.

502
00:20:39,279 --> 00:20:40,614
I LOOKED AT YOUR RECORD

503
00:20:40,614 --> 00:20:42,575
AND YOU'VE DONE
SOME PRETTY WEIRD STUFF.

504
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:44,451
YEAH, WE'LL TALK AT DINNER.

505
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:46,871
OKAY. SO I'LL COME BY
IN A COUPLE HOURS

506
00:20:46,871 --> 00:20:48,039
AND PICK YOU UP?

507
00:20:48,039 --> 00:20:49,749
ALL RIGHT.
I CAN'T WAIT.

508
00:20:49,749 --> 00:20:51,959
I'M NOT GOING TO JUST
TAKE YOU OUT FOR DOUGHNUTS.

509
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:56,172
( laughing )

510
00:20:56,172 --> 00:20:57,464
HE HAS A GUN.

511
00:21:03,721 --> 00:21:07,058
I'D LIKE TO RETURN THIS COUCH.
I'M NOT SATISFIED WITH IT.

512
00:21:12,188 --> 00:21:15,482
YOU WANT TO RETURN
THIS COUCH?

513
00:21:15,482 --> 00:21:19,695
IT'S CUT IN HALF.

514
00:21:19,695 --> 00:21:21,614
THAT'S WHAT I'M TELLING YOU.

515
00:21:21,614 --> 00:21:23,157
DID YOU CUT THIS
COUCH IN HALF?

516
00:21:25,283 --> 00:21:29,663
THIS COUCH IS CUT IN HALF.

517
00:21:29,663 --> 00:21:33,709
I WOULD LIKE TO EXCHANGE IT
FOR ONE THAT IS NOT CUT IN HALF.

518
00:21:34,835 --> 00:21:36,587
YOU'RE TELLING
ME THIS COUCH

519
00:21:36,587 --> 00:21:38,547
WAS DELIVERED
TO YOU LIKE THIS?

520
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:41,259
LOOK, I'M A REASONABLE MAN.

521
00:21:41,259 --> 00:21:44,720
I WILL ACCEPT STORE CREDIT.

522
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:46,889
I'LL GIVE YOU
STORE CREDIT

523
00:21:46,889 --> 00:21:49,433
IN THE AMOUNT
OF FOUR DOLLARS.

524
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:53,938
I WILL TAKE IT.

